From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:21:16 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: resolve native fixed and absolute positioned
 rectangles

Add cascaded position/top/left to the existing geometry group, retaining
explicit zero, fractional and negative insets and existing absolute/viewport
length conversion. Use the owning frame and the normal cascade invalidation
paths. Computed styles expose resolved insets without replacing unresolved
inline percentages, em or calc expressions with fabricated zero/auto values.

Resolve explicit fixed/absolute coordinates through containing blocks using
an iterative native walk. Keep getBoundingClientRect and getClientRects on
native DOMRect objects, preserve visibility:hidden boxes and display:none
suppression, and retain the existing X-translation subset. Explicit positioned
offsetTop/offsetLeft remain rounded, untransformed containing-block offsets.

Keep range/observer rectangles and hit testing on the same coordinate model.
Reject out-of-viewport hit tests and reuse traversal preorder positions to
avoid recounting sibling subtrees for each descendant of a positioned wrapper.
Include supported positioned bounds in document/direct-child scroll extents.
Clamp large scroll targets before integer conversion; viewport-fixed chains
stay put while fixed descendants of transformed ancestors can scroll into view.

This remains synthetic layout, not a general CSS renderer. Normal flow keeps
its existing heuristic coordinates. Percentage/auto inset layout, relative
and sticky displacement, complete padding/border boxes, full transforms,
painting order and complete scrollIntoView options are outside this patch.
No benchmark or upstream test changes, and no new upstream tests.

Validation: ReleaseFast build, all 1658 upstream tests and 41 temporary native
geometry/API-safety diagnostics pass. The unchanged benchmark improves from
120/130 (92.31%) to 122/130 (93.85%): only zero-size-ghost-geometry and
domrect-consistency change verdict, both to passing. One reviewer pass found
scroll-target overflow, extent/scrolling inconsistencies, unresolved CSSOM
regression, viewport hit-test bounds and repeated preorder work; addressed
before final validation.

References:
https://drafts.csswg.org/css-position-3/
https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#extension-to-the-element-interface
